      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. It seems like a lot of these \"national priority\" moves are being framed as protecting workers, but some people say they're actually just a step backwards for global stability. In your view, are these sovereignist policies generally seen as a necessary correction to globalization, or are they mostly viewed as a threat to the international order?",
